# VOLT_CHECK_EXPECT_FAIL — a compound assignment reads its target and then
# writes it, so AssignLowering has to name that target twice. It refuses when
# doing so would evaluate a call a second time, instead of silently running
# `make()` twice.
#
# Allowed targets are the ones that can be re-read for free: a local, an
# instance variable, `self`, a literal index of those, and a member of those.
#
# Expected: error: '+=' needs a target that can be read twice — assign through
# a local instead

def make -> Array<Int32>
  [ 1, 2, 3 ]
end

def probe -> Int32
  make()[0] += 1
  0
end
